# CRUD Module Patterns

## Standard CRUD Structure
Every CRUD module should follow this pattern based on [src/features/master-data/role/](mdc:src/features/master-data/role/):

```
features/[module-name]/
├── components/
│   ├── modal-add-[module].tsx
│   ├── modal-edit-[module].tsx
│   └── [other-components].tsx
├── hooks/
│   ├── useGetAll[Module].tsx
│   ├── useMutateAdd[Module].tsx
│   ├── useMutateEdit[Module].tsx
│   └── useMutateDelete[Module].tsx
├── types.ts
└── page-[module].tsx
```

## React Query Hook Patterns
- **GET Hook**: `useGetAll[Module]` - for fetching data with pagination, search, and filters
- **CREATE Hook**: `useMutateAdd[Module]` - for creating new records
- **UPDATE Hook**: `useMutateEdit[Module]` - for updating existing records
- **DELETE Hook**: `useMutateDelete[Module]` - for deleting records

## Form Integration
- **React Hook Form** with **Zod** validation (see [src/features/master-data/role/components/modal-add-role.tsx](mdc:src/features/master-data/role/components/modal-add-role.tsx))
- **Form Schema**: Define validation rules using Zod
- **Form State**: Use `useForm` hook with `zodResolver`

## Page Component Pattern
- **Search & Filter**: Implement debounced search using [useDebounceCallback.tsx](mdc:src/hooks/useDebounceCallback.tsx)
- **Data Table**: Use Mantine Table component with pagination
- **Modal Management**: State management for add/edit/delete modals
- **Success/Error Handling**: Use Mantine notifications for user feedback

## Type Definitions
- **Base Type**: `typeData[Module]` with standard fields (id, isActive, name, timestamps, audit fields)
- **Form Schema**: `Add[Module]Schema` and `Edit[Module]Schema` using Zod inference
- **API Response**: Use `typeDataCommonResponse<T>` wrapper for consistent API responses
